    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d446">

                <pb facs="0483" n="471" sameAs="frus:frus1945v08/pg471"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.00/12–245: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Murray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-12-02T10:00:00+03:25">December 2,
                            1945—10 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 3—7:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1041. Foreign Office has confirmed report published yesterday that all Soviet
                    military units still in Tehran have been withdrawn from city proper but says
                    they are encamped only few miles outside.</p>
                <p>Sent to Dept as 1041, repeated to Moscow 308, London 110.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Murray</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
